{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ESNext"],
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["bun-types"],
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  // A WHITELIST, so *.workflow.ts at the repo root stays out: those are akari
  // dispatch scripts, not product code, and they run under a host that provides
  // `agent`, `phase`, `parallel` and a top-level `return`, which tsc reports as
  // errors on a file that ships nothing.
  //
  // scripts/ IS product code and belongs in: onboarding is how a new agent gets
  // into Slack at all, and the live smoke is the only check that talks to Slack.
  // It sat outside this list by accident, sharing the exclusion written for the
  // workflow files, and a reference to a variable I had just deleted passed a
  // green tsc and crashed onboarding at runtime.
  "include": ["src", "test", "scripts"]
}
